[06/08/26 13:02:25] INFO     Transcription:  Imagine a large         base.py:98
                             rectangle split into two smaller                  
                             rectangles side by side. One smaller              
                             rectangle has width 4 and the other has           
                             width 3 and both share the same height            
                             v. You can find the total area in two             
                             ways, multiply v by the full width of             
                             7, giving 7v. Or add the two smaller              
                             areas, 4v plus 3v, which also gives 7v.           
                             Both methods agree and that agreement             
                             is the distributive property in action.           
