[06/08/26 13:03:03] INFO     Transcription:  The distributive        base.py:98
                             property states that a number                     
                             multiplied by a sum equals the sum of             
                             that number multiplied by each part               
                             separately. So 3 times the quantity x             
                             plus 4 equals 3 times x plus 3 times 4,           
                             which gives 3x plus 12. We must not add           
                             the terms inside the bracket first. We            
                             must distribute the multiplication                
                             across every term inside. Then, after             
                             distributing, we collect any like terms           
                             that appear.                                      
